summary:
- topic: SPHS Marching Band Recognition
  text: The South Portland High School Marching Band was celebrated for winning a
    gold medal at the Maine Band Directors Association state finals. The band director
    highlighted the extensive dedication and resilience of the 41 students and 10
    staff members, emphasizing their journey from summer camp to state-level success.
- topic: FY2026 Budget Outlook
  text: The Finance Director presented the FY2026 end-of-year projection, indicating
    a potential $337,000 deficit under normal circumstances. However, a one-time geothermal
    energy tax credit of $815,000 is expected to create a surplus, preventing the
    depletion of the district's fund balance this fiscal year. The report warned that
    rising costs and the future absence of this buffer necessitate careful financial
    planning for FY27 and beyond.
- topic: South Portland Schools Education Foundation Update
  text: An update was provided on the progress of establishing an independent South
    Portland Schools Education Foundation. The committee, comprising community partners
    and district staff, is working towards a July 2026 launch to raise funds for non-district
    associated costs, leveraging partnerships with experts and the University of Maine
    Law School.
- topic: Middle School Field Remediation
  text: The Director of Operations presented findings from soil testing at the South
    Portland Middle School field, revealing significant issues like low organic matter,
    compaction, and nutrient deficiencies. A five-step remediation plan was outlined,
    but Board members expressed strong frustration with the original contractor's
    poor work and advocated for them to cover the costs of the necessary repairs.
- topic: SPTA Contract Ratification
  text: "The Board unanimously ratified the FY 2025-28 South Portland Teachers\u2019\
    \ Association (SPTA) contract. Board members expressed gratitude to both negotiation\
    \ teams for their collaborative efforts, acknowledging the positive impact of\
    \ the agreement on teacher morale and stability."
- topic: Policy JJIF Approval (Concussion Management)
  text: Policy JJIF, concerning the management of concussions and other head injuries,
    was approved after a second reading. Board members noted the importance of the
    policy and expressed intentions to broaden its scope in the future to include
    non-athletic activities.
- topic: SPESPA Contract Negotiations
  text: During public comment, representatives from the SPTA and SPESPA urged the
    Board to prioritize and expedite negotiations for the SPESPA (Support Professionals)
    contract. Speakers emphasized the vital role of ed techs, clerks, and office managers,
    advocating for fair pay and conditions to ensure their continued dedication and
    the district's overall well-being.
- topic: Board Member Farewell Remarks
  text: Several Board members, including Chair Tandy Ratliff and member Susan Rauscher,
    delivered heartfelt farewell remarks as this was their last regular meeting before
    upcoming elections. They reflected on their service, thanked colleagues and staff,
    and expressed optimism for the future of the South Portland School Department.
